From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] JsonLib: fix RELEASE build of lex_unget_unsave

RedfishCrtLib maps assert() to EDK2's ASSERT(), and current MdePkg
defines the MDEPKG_NDEBUG flavor of ASSERT as (VOID)(Expression) - the
expression is still compiled, just not acted on. jansson's
lex_unget_unsave() guards the declaration and assignment of "d" with
"#ifndef NDEBUG" while the assert referencing it stays, so a RELEASE
build (-DMDEPKG_NDEBUG -DNDEBUG per RPi5.dsc) fails with:

  load.c:340:18: error: 'd' undeclared (first use in this function)

Declare and assign unconditionally. strbuffer_pop() must run for its
side effect in all flavors anyway, and the INF already passes
-Wno-unused-but-set-variable for GCC.

Upstream-Status: Submittable [RedfishPkg vs MdePkg ASSERT change]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/RedfishPkg/Library/JsonLib/load.c b/RedfishPkg/Library/JsonLib/load.c
index 1a3b4a6..a911f62 100644
--- a/RedfishPkg/Library/JsonLib/load.c
+++ b/RedfishPkg/Library/JsonLib/load.c
@@ -325,18 +325,16 @@ lex_unget_unsave (
   )
 {
   if ((c != STREAM_STATE_EOF) && (c != STREAM_STATE_ERROR)) {
-    /* Since we treat warnings as errors, when assertions are turned
-     * off the "d" variable would be set but never used. Which is
-     * treated as an error by GCC.
+    /* "d" must exist in all build flavors: RedfishCrtLib maps assert()
+     * to EDK2's ASSERT(), whose MDEPKG_NDEBUG form is (VOID)(Expression)
+     * - the expression is still compiled, so an NDEBUG-guarded
+     * declaration breaks RELEASE builds. The unconditional assignment is
+     * fine: strbuffer_pop() must run for its side effect either way, and
+     * this INF already passes -Wno-unused-but-set-variable.
      */
- #ifndef NDEBUG
     char  d;
- #endif
     stream_unget (&lex->stream, c);
- #ifndef NDEBUG
-    d =
- #endif
-    strbuffer_pop (&lex->saved_text);
+    d = strbuffer_pop (&lex->saved_text);
     assert (c == d);
   }
 }
